{"name":"Kowloon","hex":"#e1d956","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Kowloon","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A region, peninsula, and urban area of Hong Kong."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Kowloon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Kowloon","blocks":[{"text":"Kowloon, formerly Kaulung, is one of the three areas of Hong Kong, along with Hong Kong Island and the New Territories. It is an urban area comprising the Kowloon Peninsula and New Kowloon. It has a population of 2,019,533 and a population density of 43,033/km2 (111,450/sq mi) in 2006. It is the smallest, second most populous, and most densely populated of the divisions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Union_Square_and_Tsim_Sha_Tsui.jpg/330px-Union_Square_and_Tsim_Sha_Tsui.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kowloon","wikidata":"Q239143"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Kowloon_City%2C_Mainland%2C_opposite_Hong_Kong.jpg/500px-Kowloon_City%2C_Mainland%2C_opposite_Hong_Kong.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Kowloon_City%2C_Mainland%2C_opposite_Hong_Kong.jpg/1280px-Kowloon_City%2C_Mainland%2C_opposite_Hong_Kong.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Kowloon_City%2C_Mainland%2C_opposite_Hong_Kong.jpg/500px-Kowloon_City%2C_Mainland%2C_opposite_Hong_Kong.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Kowloon c. 1868, depicting the Qing-era Kowloon Walled City and Lion Rock (in the background)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKowloon_City%2C_Mainland%2C_opposite_Hong_Kong.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Victoria_City_and_K